course: dictionary
lesson: 6986
title: Words about the Pope
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Papal is an adjective, so it describes a noun. It tells you that something belongs to, or comes from, the Pope, the head of the Roman Catholic Church. When you meet it, look for the noun it describes.
explain: «Prince Danylo received a royal crown from a papal envoy.» An envoy is a messenger, and papal tells you whose messenger he was. Swap in your meaning: a messenger of the Pope fits the sentence, so your meaning works.
explain: «The Papal States cover a large part of central Italy.» The word states is a clue that this is about lands, and papal tells you those lands are linked with the Pope. Read the whole sentence, not just the hard word.
fact: Papal means to do with the Pope, the head of the Roman Catholic Church.
fact: «Papal» is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a visit, a letter or a palace.
fact: «Papal envoy» means a messenger of the Pope.
fact: «Papal States» were lands in central Italy; by 1870 they had been lost to Italy, and only the tiny Vatican City remains.
fact: A good check is to swap in "of the Pope": a papal visit is a visit of the Pope.
exercise: «Prince Danylo received a royal crown from a papal envoy.» What does papal mean here? | To do with a king | To do with the sea | Made of paper | *To do with the Pope
exercise: Papal means to do with which person? | A teacher | *The Pope, head of the Roman Catholic Church | A pilot | A prince
exercise: «The Papal States cover a large part of central Italy.» Find and copy the word that tells you the states are linked with the Pope. | central | States | *Papal | Italy
test: Which phrase means a messenger of the Pope? | a central plain | a Roman bridge | *a papal envoy | a royal crown
test: What does a papal letter mean? | *A letter to do with the Pope | A letter written in a hurry | A letter about the weather | A letter with a royal seal
exam: Which word best fits? «The ___ palace stood in the middle of the old city.» | *papal | barely | sunny | curt
</br>
